  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q36-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $P(x)=6x^3+8x^2+8x+9$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q36-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the quotient and remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $2x^2+3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q(x)=3x+4$, $R(x)=-x-3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(6x^3+8x^2+8x+9)-3x(2x^2+3)&=8x^2-x+9\\\\(8x^2-x+9)-4(2x^2+3)&=-x-3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe remainder has degree less than 2.\n\n$$Q(x)=3x+4,\\qquad R(x)=-x-3.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q36-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find $a$ and $b$ such that $6x^3+8x^2+ax+b$ has remainder 0 when divided by $2x^2+3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p8-q36-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a=9,\\quad b=12",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p8-q36-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The remainder is ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(a-9)x+(b-12)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; set both coefficients to zero.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(6x^3+8x^2+ax+b)-3x(2x^2+3)&=8x^2+(a-9)x+b\\\\\\bigl(8x^2+(a-9)x+b\\bigr)-4(2x^2+3)&=(a-9)x+(b-12)\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor the remainder to be the zero polynomial, both coefficients must be zero:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a-9&=0\\\\a&=9\\\\b-12&=0\\\\b&=12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
